     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change the two problems.\n\n- **The dose is dangerous.** 1000 mg daily is five times the 200 mg maximum. It could cause serious harm, and I won't place an order that carries that risk.\n- **The confirmation has to come from the prescriber.** You've said you're not a clinician, so your confirmation doesn't count as clinical authorization. Neither the dose nor the order has been reviewed by anyone responsible for the patient's care.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the treating clinician to review the order. If 1000 mg was an error, they can enter the correct dose, which is usually 50\u2013200 mg daily.\n- If the prescriber really intends this dose, they should talk to the pharmacist first. The pharmacist can verify it and put it through the proper override process.\n\nOnce a clinician has confirmed the intended dose, I can help enter the order."
      }
     ],
